<Base title="About · Ujwal" description="BA x Design Engineer generalist — analysis, prototyping, delivery." current="about">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:34px;font-weight:400;margin:6px 0">Generalist at the intersection of analysis, design and delivery.</h1>
    <p>I work as Business Analyst / Product Owner who can also prototype and reason about systems. On Horizon I owned what the platform had to do — requirements, scope, trade-offs, change control — while a team of 1 SM, 1 designer, 1 DevOps, 1 QA (from April) and 5 full-stack devs built it.</p>

    <div class="g3">
      <div class="c"><h3>Analysis</h3><p>Discovery, requirements, KYC/suitability funnels, privilege matrices (14 modules), audit &amp; compliance scope, Jira workflows.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Design engineering</h3><p>Same-mental-model flows, role-specific dashboards, HTML/CSS prototypes, e-signature template thinking, status-as-communication.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Delivery</h3><p>Scrum 2-week sprints, backlog refinement with client, 3 change requests scoped in writing, UAT → prod, migration &amp; rebrand holds.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Skills matrix — derived from Horizon</h2>
    <div class="g2">
      <div class="c"><h3>Product &amp; domain</h3><p>Secondary-market lifecycle: Submitted → Approved → Subscribed → Allocated. Investor tiers Lite → Plus → Pro, joint/IRA/entity accounts, fund closure FIFO, unit batches &amp; cost basis.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Decisions I owned</h3><p>Tiers as funnel, manual wire over failed processor path, native e-sign over 10s vendor screen, K8s cost cut $1.5k→&lt;$800, CSV user migration now / docs later.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Platform literacy</h3><p>Cognito + RBAC checked live, KMS envelope + field-level encryption, RabbitMQ + Redis pub/sub + SSE, Linkerd mTLS, OTel → Grafana, SonarQube + canary.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Ways of working</h3><p>One source of truth in Jira, handover checklists, sizing sign-offs, versioned user manual as knowledge base for future assistant.</p></div>
    </div>

